From 0255f415a41505f2acb394c2ea19f6b2cd3d3a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 01:24:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplmesh: Add HE capabilities processing, UHR mode reporting,
 and htmode config fix

Changes include:
- Added X_QCA_UhrMode field to Radio object in DM schema
- Implemented set_ap_he_capabilities() to process 0x88 TLV
- Fixed htmode reading to support new UCI format (wireless.radio0_band0.htmode)
- Added UHR mode detection and reporting from QCA WiFi-8 Capabilities TLV
- Fixed WiFi6 MCS/NSS parsing and NSS encoding (IEEE 802.11ax uses 0-based encoding)
- Updated qmesh-lib to read UHR mode from DM
- Updated steering app to detect and use UHR mode capabilities
- Agent only registers a radio's UHR flag when its htmode is actually UHR;
  if none qualify, the QCA WiFi-8 Capabilities TLV is omitted from the AP
  Capability Report entirely
- Controller clears X_QCA_UhrMode/Wifi8Capable for all of an agent's radios
  when the TLV is absent, so a UHR -> non-UHR htmode transition (e.g. to
  EHT) doesn't leave a stale X_QCA_UhrMode=true in the DM
- Added bpl_cfg_get_radio_htmode() stubs to the dm (WHM/UGW), rdk, and linux
  bpl backends - it was only implemented in cfg/uci/bpl_cfg_wifi.cpp, and
  USE_PRPLMESH_WHM builds substitute cfg/dm/bpl_cfg_wifi.cpp for that file,
  causing beerocks_agent to fail at link time with an undefined reference
  to beerocks::bpl::bpl_cfg_get_radio_htmode

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
